              heading: 'Part 4',
              text: 'This is a popular folk art form in Odisha. From 1912–1948, artists participated in the Olympics. It included architecture, literature, music, painting, and sculpture competitions. Baron Pierre de Coubertin, the founder of the modern Olympics, felt that all art inspired by sport could be eligible to participate. These were legitimate medal events, and over medals were awarded. What do you think? Should it be brought back? Theatre Trivia — Art in Olympics! Theatre Theatre.indd Theatre.indd ASSESSMENT — : Look Around Competencies C-4.1: Recognises elements of drama and movement in nature and describes their artistic qualities C-4.2: Demonstrates curiosity towards local art forms and culture CG Competencies Learning Outcomes Teacher Self 4.1 Replicates elements observed in nature in detail 4.1 Relates one’s role to an unknown situation through imagination 4.1 Provides feedback on others’ acts based on content and technique 4.2 Understands the concept of animals as the core idea of a folk form 4.2 Relates to the story in the folk form and asks questions 4.2 Shares examples of other art forms involving animals or tries to create their own Overall participation in class Teacher’s feedback on student’s strengths Teacher’s feedback on areas of improvement Any other observation Bansuri • Grade Theatre.indd Theatre.indd Activity for assessment (example) Criteria for assessment Individual • The child is asked to pick an animal of their choice. • Build and narrate a story around the animal. • Enact as the animal in the story (say a few lines with emotion and action).',
